1
00:00:01,281 --> 00:00:03,191
Then I'm counting on you, Director Joo.

2
00:00:04,691 --> 00:00:05,751
You can count on me.

3
00:00:12,061 --> 00:00:13,601
Why is this so difficult?

4
00:00:14,301 --> 00:00:17,071
Cha Seok Jin is so difficult.

5
00:00:17,801 --> 00:00:20,501
The harder something is to get, the more it's worth.

6
00:00:21,871 --> 00:00:25,471
Letting Cha Seok Jin into your life isn't a bad investment.

7
00:00:25,911 --> 00:00:29,411
Even so, how am I supposed to handle all this stress?

8
00:00:29,511 --> 00:00:30,581
I'm home.

9
00:00:31,581 --> 00:00:33,021
The Chairman's home.

10
00:00:33,551 --> 00:00:34,721
Pull yourself together and come out.

11
00:00:36,181 --> 00:00:38,591
Whatever. This is so annoying.

12
00:00:40,021 --> 00:00:42,891
Gosh, ma'am. I see you left the office late.

13
00:00:44,291 --> 00:00:45,961
I had to meet with someone.

14
00:00:47,501 --> 00:00:48,501
Where's Hae Ra?

15
00:00:48,761 --> 00:00:50,131
She's in her room.

16
00:00:50,571 --> 00:00:52,231
I don't think she's feeling very well.

17
00:00:52,801 --> 00:00:53,801
Really?

18
00:00:54,401 --> 00:00:55,601
Is it serious?

19
00:01:03,811 --> 00:01:04,981
Tell her to get plenty of rest.

20
00:01:05,411 --> 00:01:07,851
Director Joo, make sure she gets some vitamins.

21
00:01:09,081 --> 00:01:10,321
Yes, of course.

22
00:01:23,131 --> 00:01:24,131
I will.

23
00:01:24,901 --> 00:01:27,641
Thank you so, so much, ma'am.

24
00:01:30,971 --> 00:01:33,741
Such a pure-hearted young woman. You rarely see that these days.

25
00:01:42,951 --> 00:01:43,951
What's that?

26
00:01:44,591 --> 00:01:47,561
It looks very nice. Is it expensive?

27
00:01:48,021 --> 00:01:50,231
No, of course not.

28
00:01:51,161 --> 00:01:52,531
Just because you're earning some money...

29
00:01:52,591 --> 00:01:54,061
doesn't mean you can spend it like water.

30
00:01:54,931 --> 00:01:56,601
Right, I won't.

31
00:01:57,301 --> 00:02:01,171
Think about when your mother was still alive.

32
00:02:02,601 --> 00:02:05,711
She would've done anything for you.

33
00:02:06,481 --> 00:02:09,081
For you, who wasn't even her own blood,

34
00:02:09,411 --> 00:02:11,981
she ignored her own son, the third-generation only son,

35
00:02:12,851 --> 00:02:15,051
and only cherished you.

36
00:02:16,221 --> 00:02:17,221
Grandma,

37
00:02:18,251 --> 00:02:20,521
I'll pay you back for everything when I succeed.

38
00:02:20,791 --> 00:02:22,561
Later? What do you mean, later?

39
00:02:23,261 --> 00:02:26,531
I might not even be alive by then.

40
00:02:30,371 --> 00:02:31,531
By the way...

41
00:02:32,831 --> 00:02:35,501
Now that your name has been cleared,

42
00:02:36,271 --> 00:02:39,941
aren't you curious about your birth mother?

43
00:02:42,511 --> 00:02:46,751
I mean, she has to be alive somewhere.

44
00:02:47,851 --> 00:02:49,851
- Mom! - What the...

45
00:02:50,951 --> 00:02:52,551
- What? Why? - Come on.

46
00:02:56,831 --> 00:02:57,991
What's wrong with you?

47
00:02:59,691 --> 00:03:01,301
Gosh, you're making me dizzy.

48
00:03:01,301 --> 00:03:04,331
Mom, that's enough.

49
00:03:05,101 --> 00:03:07,401
It hasn't been that long since Eun Seol was exonerated.

50
00:03:08,301 --> 00:03:10,411
If Hee Jung saw you acting like this,

51
00:03:10,471 --> 00:03:11,971
she'd be heartbroken.

52
00:03:12,471 --> 00:03:14,311
While Hee Jung was alive, she might've put up...

53
00:03:14,311 --> 00:03:15,841
with a mother-in-law like you,

54
00:03:15,911 --> 00:03:16,911
but in the afterlife?

55
00:03:16,951 --> 00:03:18,581
She won't stand for it.

56
00:03:19,981 --> 00:03:22,181
You'll get what's coming to you, Mom.

57
00:03:22,451 --> 00:03:24,591
What? What's coming to me?

58
00:03:24,591 --> 00:03:25,991
You brat!

59
00:03:26,051 --> 00:03:27,891
You'd be happy if your mother got what she deserves.

60
00:03:27,961 --> 00:03:30,161
That's why you need to be nice to Eun Seol.

61
00:03:30,931 --> 00:03:32,831
Aren't you afraid of divine punishment, Mom?

62
00:03:32,891 --> 00:03:34,631
Afraid? Don't be ridiculous.

63
00:03:35,231 --> 00:03:36,571
Is that what you're afraid of?

64
00:03:37,201 --> 00:03:38,571
What I'm more afraid of...

65
00:03:38,731 --> 00:03:42,701
is you and your son inheriting that good-for-nothing laziness.

66
00:03:43,411 --> 00:03:46,441
It's not some great legacy to be passed down,

67
00:03:46,511 --> 00:03:48,841
but it has run through this family for generations.

68
00:03:49,311 --> 00:03:51,881
Anyway, the men in this godforsaken family...

69
00:03:52,881 --> 00:03:56,021
have never earned a single dime with their own two hands.

70
00:03:57,991 --> 00:04:01,491
I guess that just means the men in our family have married well.

71
00:04:01,561 --> 00:04:03,831
Me, Father, all of us, right?

72
00:04:04,161 --> 00:04:06,331
Although, Dad didn't do as well as I did.

73
00:04:08,361 --> 00:04:12,571
Still, he got a free ride for most of his life.

74
00:04:12,631 --> 00:04:16,841
Right. Some great genes you have, you brat.

75
00:04:17,311 --> 00:04:18,311
I'm...

76
00:04:18,371 --> 00:04:19,771
not afraid of anything.

77
00:04:21,041 --> 00:04:23,181
If we can just find Eun Seol's birth mother,

78
00:04:23,751 --> 00:04:24,981
it's a whopping...

79
00:04:26,081 --> 00:04:28,181
half a million dollars. Half a million.

80
00:04:28,381 --> 00:04:29,721
I'm telling you, it's not happening!

81
00:04:31,051 --> 00:04:32,551
If you dare mention...

82
00:04:33,021 --> 00:04:36,291
her birth mother again in front of Eun Seol,

83
00:04:36,861 --> 00:04:38,231
I'll never see you again.

84
00:04:43,631 --> 00:04:45,771
Go ahead and try to stop me.

85
00:04:45,831 --> 00:04:47,471
I won't be silenced.

86
00:04:48,001 --> 00:04:49,171
We're talking about 500,000 dollars.

87
00:04:54,741 --> 00:04:55,741
Dad.

88
00:04:56,211 --> 00:04:57,211
What are you up to?

89
00:04:57,881 --> 00:04:58,981
Sketching.

90
00:04:59,351 --> 00:05:00,821
I'm working on a rough draft for a design.

91
00:05:03,321 --> 00:05:04,951
It's good to see you so busy.

92
00:05:05,751 --> 00:05:09,891
Hey, just forget everything Grandma said earlier.

93
00:05:09,991 --> 00:05:12,931
It's okay. She only said it because she's worried about me.

94
00:05:13,161 --> 00:05:15,401
Right. Don't take it to heart.

95
00:05:15,461 --> 00:05:17,031
Just let it all go, okay?

96
00:05:18,271 --> 00:05:20,441
Right. But Dad...

97
00:05:22,501 --> 00:05:23,511
I...

98
00:05:24,341 --> 00:05:26,981
want to try and track down my birth mother.

99
00:05:27,041 --> 00:05:29,211
Wait, really?

100
00:05:29,811 --> 00:05:31,611
But not right now.

101
00:05:32,251 --> 00:05:33,481
Right now,

102
00:05:33,551 --> 00:05:36,151
I want to get back the ten years I lost.

103
00:05:37,151 --> 00:05:40,461
The real killer has been caught, and my retrial will be held soon.

104
00:05:41,321 --> 00:05:42,391
For the first time,

105
00:05:42,461 --> 00:05:44,691
I feel like the second act of my life is beginning.

106
00:05:46,391 --> 00:05:49,231
After I find the real me that I lost for ten years...

107
00:05:50,131 --> 00:05:51,231
Then...

108
00:05:52,101 --> 00:05:54,741
that's when I'm going to find my birth mother.

109
00:05:56,071 --> 00:05:57,071
Okay.

110
00:05:57,771 --> 00:05:59,241
If anyone can do it, you can.

111
00:05:59,641 --> 00:06:01,911
Of course. We know who you take after.

112
00:06:03,511 --> 00:06:05,381
And don't forget.

113
00:06:06,051 --> 00:06:07,351
Behind you,

114
00:06:07,851 --> 00:06:09,851
your dad...

115
00:06:09,921 --> 00:06:12,651
and your brother will be right there.

116
00:06:13,121 --> 00:06:14,191
Got it?

117
00:06:14,421 --> 00:06:16,491
Yes. Of course.

118
00:06:16,591 --> 00:06:19,391
With such a dependable dad like you, what do I have to worry about?

119
00:06:20,101 --> 00:06:21,701
From now on, whenever things get tough,

120
00:06:21,761 --> 00:06:23,671
I'm going to lean on you for everything.

121
00:06:24,031 --> 00:06:25,301
And on Eun Guk, too.

122
00:06:25,901 --> 00:06:26,941
Good.

123
00:06:27,601 --> 00:06:28,601
For everything.

124
00:06:45,391 --> 00:06:46,761
(Cheongma)

125
00:06:48,461 --> 00:06:50,091
Is Ms. Ko not here yet?

126
00:06:50,661 --> 00:06:51,961
She seems to be busy these days.

127
00:06:52,031 --> 00:06:53,701
One might think she's pounding the pavement.

128
00:06:54,161 --> 00:06:56,401
From shoe repair shops to master shoemakers,

129
00:06:56,771 --> 00:06:59,271
she's been running all over town and is never in the office.

130
00:07:00,031 --> 00:07:01,841
Let's start the meeting on time.

131
00:07:02,301 --> 00:07:04,841
It's five minutes before the hour. Let's just get started.

132
00:07:07,111 --> 00:07:08,641
I'm sorry I'm late.

133
00:07:08,711 --> 00:07:11,511
We still have five minutes left. You should prepare for the meeting.

134
00:07:12,151 --> 00:07:13,151
Right.

135
00:07:16,551 --> 00:07:18,191
All right, as per company guidelines,

136
00:07:18,251 --> 00:07:20,461
the first concept drafts for the Shoejoy internal competition...

137
00:07:20,561 --> 00:07:23,391
will be shared with the entire team for a cross-check.

138
00:07:23,661 --> 00:07:25,561
Please focus your review on the design's intent...

139
00:07:25,561 --> 00:07:27,001
and its feasibility.

140
00:07:27,301 --> 00:07:28,331
Let's begin.

141
00:07:29,531 --> 00:07:31,871
(Head of Design Team, Kang Hae Ra)

142
00:07:39,541 --> 00:07:41,781
The competition is right around the corner,

143
00:07:42,211 --> 00:07:44,151
yet you don't have a solid first draft.

144
00:07:44,211 --> 00:07:45,511
That says it all, doesn't it?

145
00:07:45,911 --> 00:07:46,951
Ms. Ko,

146
00:07:47,351 --> 00:07:48,521
can you actually get this done?

147
00:07:49,081 --> 00:07:51,491
Yes, it's doable, Ms. Kang.

148
00:07:52,921 --> 00:07:56,491
People with tough upbringings can be so defiant.

149
00:07:56,931 --> 00:07:58,361
They assume that putting in long hours...

150
00:07:58,431 --> 00:07:59,861
is the same as having grit.

151
00:07:59,931 --> 00:08:02,201
They fool themselves into believing they're actually hardworking.

152
00:08:04,331 --> 00:08:05,331
But...

153
00:08:05,731 --> 00:08:07,201
it's all just false bravado.

154
00:08:07,801 --> 00:08:10,341
Crashing and burning after trying your best is just sad,

155
00:08:10,771 --> 00:08:11,841
so don't overdo it.

156
00:08:13,041 --> 00:08:16,641
Failing because you're overconfident seems even more pathetic to me.

157
00:08:17,311 --> 00:08:18,311
What?

158
00:08:19,481 --> 00:08:20,781
Hey, it's already lunchtime.

159
00:08:21,951 --> 00:08:24,051
Well then, enjoy your lunch, everyone.

160
00:08:38,401 --> 00:08:40,001
I think I'm a little twisted.

161
00:08:40,841 --> 00:08:42,801
When someone tries to put me down,

162
00:08:43,001 --> 00:08:44,871
I get this strange desire to fight back.

163
00:08:46,471 --> 00:08:47,481
What happened?

164
00:08:47,641 --> 00:08:49,811
Did Team Leader Kang tick you off again today?

165
00:08:50,041 --> 00:08:52,381
Well, it's nothing new.

166
00:08:53,281 --> 00:08:54,281
Still...

167
00:08:54,681 --> 00:08:57,621
It makes me angry, but I'm not intimidated.

168
00:08:58,291 --> 00:09:00,691
I guess going through worse toughens you up like that.

169
00:09:01,961 --> 00:09:04,761
Once the moment passes, I find it bearable.

170
00:09:07,561 --> 00:09:08,831
I like how resilient you are.

171
00:09:19,641 --> 00:09:23,341
Lately, I've been feeling like I've been born again,

172
00:09:23,751 --> 00:09:25,611
so I have a huge appetite.

173
00:09:26,311 --> 00:09:27,321
Have your fill.

174
00:09:27,721 --> 00:09:29,751
I prefer seeing you like this, Eun Seol.

175
00:09:39,961 --> 00:09:42,131
How are things with the internal competition?

176
00:09:43,001 --> 00:09:44,231
Based on the interim score,

177
00:09:44,301 --> 00:09:46,371
Team Leader Kang appears to have the upper hand.

178
00:09:47,071 --> 00:09:49,771
And it seems Ko Eun Seol's first draft is lacking.

179
00:09:51,741 --> 00:09:53,071
Our Hae Ra did graduate...

180
00:09:53,141 --> 00:09:55,581
from one of the top three design schools in France.

181
00:09:56,111 --> 00:09:58,411
How can she be compared to some kid with no pedigree?

182
00:09:59,311 --> 00:10:01,781
Of course. You can't ignore one's upbringing...

183
00:10:01,851 --> 00:10:02,951
and early education.

184
00:10:03,081 --> 00:10:05,721
Keep me updated on the Shoejoy situation.

185
00:10:05,921 --> 00:10:07,091
I want to use this chance...

186
00:10:07,121 --> 00:10:08,891
to objectively evaluate Hae Ra's skills.

187
00:10:09,591 --> 00:10:11,391
Yes, I'll do that.

188
00:10:11,791 --> 00:10:13,831
- Then... - Director Joo.

189
00:10:15,201 --> 00:10:19,031
- Yes? - It's about Jong Min.

190
00:10:20,171 --> 00:10:22,371
Right. You mean Bae Jong Min?

191
00:10:23,141 --> 00:10:26,271
Something about the incident with Jong Min feels off.

192
00:10:26,511 --> 00:10:30,351
I'm sure someone deliberately stirred things up.

193
00:10:31,351 --> 00:10:35,321
Can you find out who's behind the affair rumour?

194
00:10:36,551 --> 00:10:39,651
Yes, I'll look into it.

195
00:10:43,891 --> 00:10:44,931
It's me.

196
00:10:45,331 --> 00:10:47,601
About Bae Jong Min that I asked about...

197
00:10:47,661 --> 00:10:49,061
Can you dig into him a little more?

198
00:10:49,261 --> 00:10:50,531
What a surprise.

199
00:10:51,101 --> 00:10:53,501
The boss is reaching out herself.

200
00:10:54,141 --> 00:10:56,371
Is Manager Na doing well?

201
00:10:56,371 --> 00:10:57,371
Yes.

202
00:10:57,571 --> 00:11:00,071
I'm calling since he went on a long business trip.

203
00:11:00,271 --> 00:11:02,881
Right, about that case.

204
00:11:03,041 --> 00:11:05,581
As I mentioned before,

205
00:11:05,951 --> 00:11:09,081
there's nothing more to dig up on this Bae Jong Min guy.

206
00:11:09,751 --> 00:11:11,891
His daily life is just too spotless.

207
00:11:12,191 --> 00:11:13,621
How should I put this?

208
00:11:13,661 --> 00:11:15,591
The man is squeaky clean.

209
00:11:15,661 --> 00:11:17,391
He's a simple man.

210
00:11:17,391 --> 00:11:18,931
Okay, I get that.

211
00:11:18,991 --> 00:11:21,601
But I'm telling you to dig deeper.

212
00:11:21,831 --> 00:11:23,131
The guy only goes between...

213
00:11:23,131 --> 00:11:26,131
the university, home, and the library. I mean...

214
00:11:26,571 --> 00:11:29,801
It's hard to fabricate something out of thin air.

215
00:11:29,901 --> 00:11:32,671
That's why I'm telling you to get back to work.

216
00:11:32,741 --> 00:11:34,111
Just send me the pieces,

217
00:11:34,111 --> 00:11:36,981
and I'll either fit them together or figure something out.

218
00:11:37,151 --> 00:11:39,481
Shouldn't you just do what you're told?

219
00:11:39,851 --> 00:11:41,051
Well, then.

220
00:11:41,681 --> 00:11:44,051
When should I start?

221
00:11:44,121 --> 00:11:45,321
Starting right now.

222
00:11:46,191 --> 00:11:48,361
Well, first things first.

223
00:11:49,191 --> 00:11:52,331
I'll need to be paid first.

224
00:11:52,891 --> 00:11:54,331
Look, the thing is,

225
00:11:54,401 --> 00:11:56,961
I can't start working until I get paid.

226
00:11:57,031 --> 00:11:58,031
Just...

227
00:12:00,471 --> 00:12:02,871
Fine. I'll wire the money.

228
00:12:10,811 --> 00:12:13,381
It's times like these I miss Manager Na.

229
00:12:15,781 --> 00:12:17,391
Tae Hoon, wish you were here.

230
00:12:29,961 --> 00:12:31,771
- What are you doing? - Oh, this.

231
00:12:31,971 --> 00:12:33,631
I'm squeezing in a workout.

232
00:12:34,271 --> 00:12:39,071
If all you do is look at muscles, they'll melt away like snow.

233
00:12:39,711 --> 00:12:41,811
You have to wake them up now and then...

234
00:12:42,341 --> 00:12:45,251
to get them all pumped up.

235
00:12:45,581 --> 00:12:47,621
You're so extra.

236
00:12:47,921 --> 00:12:48,921
Two.

237
00:12:49,981 --> 00:12:51,951
Move. You're kicking up dust.

238
00:12:54,161 --> 00:12:56,421
- Oh, my aching back. - Welcome!

239
00:12:57,191 --> 00:13:00,261
Grandma. Here, sit here.

240
00:13:00,501 --> 00:13:03,871
Gosh, it's so hot. Why is it so hot today?

241
00:13:04,031 --> 00:13:05,371
I'm being steamed alive.

242
00:13:05,371 --> 00:13:07,071
- What am I, a cob of corn? - I'll...

243
00:13:07,701 --> 00:13:09,141
I'll get you a nice, cold coffee.

244
00:13:09,141 --> 00:13:10,271
- Okay. - Just a moment.

245
00:13:10,271 --> 00:13:12,241
Make mine a sweet instant coffee.

246
00:13:12,541 --> 00:13:14,841
We don't have sweet instant coffee here.

247
00:13:14,911 --> 00:13:17,881
Just make it sweet for her. Add a lot of syrup.

248
00:13:18,481 --> 00:13:20,051
Or should I do it, boss?

249
00:13:22,621 --> 00:13:24,921
Gosh, why is this so sweet?

250
00:13:25,291 --> 00:13:27,361
You like sweet things.

251
00:13:27,461 --> 00:13:30,561
How is sweet coffee the same as a sweet cookie?

252
00:13:31,561 --> 00:13:33,491
You charge money for this?

253
00:13:33,491 --> 00:13:35,661
Of course we charge for it.

254
00:13:36,161 --> 00:13:37,571
As if that'd be for free.

255
00:13:37,571 --> 00:13:39,931
Goodness, you have no shame.

256
00:13:40,171 --> 00:13:41,741
- What? - Grandma,

257
00:13:41,741 --> 00:13:43,911
the one right beside it isn't quite as sweet.

258
00:13:43,971 --> 00:13:45,411
This one? Okay.

259
00:13:46,111 --> 00:13:51,011
That'll be 14 dollars for the coffee and cookies.

260
00:13:51,911 --> 00:13:53,251
She's actually charging me?

261
00:13:54,651 --> 00:13:56,421
What a total crook.

262
00:13:56,581 --> 00:13:58,021
What did you say?

263
00:13:58,191 --> 00:14:00,661
Boss, just take it out of my paycheck.

264
00:14:02,321 --> 00:14:03,561
Grandma, here.

265
00:14:20,541 --> 00:14:22,911
Chief, you haven't left yet?

266
00:14:23,381 --> 00:14:24,681
What about you? Aren't you leaving?

267
00:14:25,251 --> 00:14:28,451
I'm just stuck on something.

268
00:14:29,751 --> 00:14:30,751
Let me see.

269
00:14:36,221 --> 00:14:39,631
If I try to include all those practical demands from the field,

270
00:14:39,691 --> 00:14:41,401
the design becomes too clunky.

271
00:14:41,931 --> 00:14:44,131
And when I try to focus on visual elegance,

272
00:14:44,201 --> 00:14:45,831
the comfort is compromised.

273
00:14:46,301 --> 00:14:48,171
Between the aesthetic and the functionality,

274
00:14:48,241 --> 00:14:50,001
it's not easy to strike a balance.

275
00:14:52,311 --> 00:14:55,741
The most important thing in a design is the designer's values.

276
00:14:56,441 --> 00:14:59,311
Of course, understanding the customer's needs is important,

277
00:14:59,811 --> 00:15:01,221
but in the end, even those needs...

278
00:15:01,581 --> 00:15:04,451
are fulfilled through the designer's interpretation...

279
00:15:04,521 --> 00:15:05,521
and philosophy.

280
00:15:06,921 --> 00:15:08,361
My interpretation?

281
00:15:08,521 --> 00:15:09,721
Have you thought about it?

282
00:15:10,091 --> 00:15:12,731
What is it you want to say through this design?

283
00:15:14,201 --> 00:15:15,961
What I want to say?

284
00:15:25,411 --> 00:15:26,411
Hey, Hae Ra.

285
00:15:26,941 --> 00:15:28,911
Seok Jin, where are you? Are you still at the office?

286
00:15:29,181 --> 00:15:31,481
I'm in the lobby. Should I come up?

287
00:15:31,751 --> 00:15:34,481
No, don't come up. I'll come down. Wait for me in the lobby.

288
00:15:35,051 --> 00:15:36,051
Okay.

289
00:15:37,321 --> 00:15:38,521
Don't work too hard.

290
00:15:38,651 --> 00:15:39,691
I'm heading out.

291
00:15:39,891 --> 00:15:41,021
Chief Cha.

292
00:15:46,391 --> 00:15:49,661
Do you really have to go right now?

293
00:15:56,201 --> 00:15:57,201
Hey.

294
00:15:57,541 --> 00:15:59,571
Seok Jin, should I just come up?

295
00:15:59,771 --> 00:16:01,381
No, I told you not to.

296
00:16:04,781 --> 00:16:07,921
If you need help, feel free to come by my office anytime.

297
00:16:22,001 --> 00:16:26,031
Get a grip, Ko Eun Seol. Now's not the time for this.

298
00:16:26,801 --> 00:16:27,801
Seriously.

299
00:16:39,011 --> 00:16:41,081
You said we were leaving together today.

300
00:16:42,121 --> 00:16:43,551
You kept me waiting for ages.

301
00:16:44,121 --> 00:16:45,321
Aren't you busy?

302
00:16:45,591 --> 00:16:47,621
Eun Seol is still back there working.

303
00:16:50,891 --> 00:16:52,391
You were with Ko Eun Seol?

304
00:16:53,531 --> 00:16:55,261
No, I just saw her on my way out.

305
00:16:56,961 --> 00:16:58,271
How are we the same?

306
00:16:58,331 --> 00:17:00,171
Why would you compare me to her?

307
00:17:00,841 --> 00:17:01,971
It's annoying.

308
00:17:02,901 --> 00:17:04,371
What's there to be annoyed about?

309
00:17:17,851 --> 00:17:20,221
What are you doing up, Ms. So Yeon?

310
00:17:20,621 --> 00:17:23,021
Hey. You're home, Mr. Seok Jin.

311
00:17:23,221 --> 00:17:25,791
Just a minute. Let me just finish this.

312
00:17:27,261 --> 00:17:28,631
I see it's a keyring.

313
00:17:28,731 --> 00:17:30,631
Who are you working so hard to make that for?

314
00:17:31,601 --> 00:17:33,271
It's a gift for someone.

315
00:17:33,971 --> 00:17:35,271
Who? Hae Ra?

316
00:17:36,471 --> 00:17:37,471
No.

317
00:17:38,211 --> 00:17:40,571
I don't like her.

318
00:17:40,881 --> 00:17:42,941
She's not nice. I can't stand her.

319
00:17:43,481 --> 00:17:45,851
Come on. I told you not to say that.

320
00:17:47,011 --> 00:17:49,021
Is the mother-in-law drama starting already?

321
00:17:50,891 --> 00:17:52,191
So who is it for, then?

322
00:17:53,391 --> 00:17:54,721
That nice lady.

323
00:17:55,621 --> 00:17:56,891
Oh, her.

324
00:17:58,191 --> 00:17:59,491
But how are you going to give it to her?

325
00:17:59,561 --> 00:18:01,731
You don't even know where she lives.

326
00:18:01,831 --> 00:18:03,231
You're right, I don't.

327
00:18:03,901 --> 00:18:05,301
What should I do?

328
00:18:05,971 --> 00:18:08,271
I really want to give this to her.

329
00:18:08,671 --> 00:18:11,341
It would suit her so well.

330
00:18:16,041 --> 00:18:17,041
Mom.

331
00:18:18,381 --> 00:18:20,351
I promise I'll find that nice lady for you.

332
00:18:21,351 --> 00:18:23,421
Really? You promise?

333
00:18:23,821 --> 00:18:25,191
Yes, I promise.

334
00:18:29,321 --> 00:18:32,591
To prevent any future in-law drama, let's all have a meal together.

335
00:18:34,131 --> 00:18:35,131
Okay.

336
00:18:36,131 --> 00:18:37,731
I mean, we'll have lunch with Hae Ra.

337
00:18:38,831 --> 00:18:40,301
Suit yourself.

338
00:18:45,811 --> 00:18:48,511
So, how's the internal competition going?

339
00:18:48,911 --> 00:18:50,341
Of course it's going well, Dad.

340
00:18:50,441 --> 00:18:52,481
I didn't study abroad for nothing, you know.

341
00:18:52,681 --> 00:18:53,881
Rightly so.

342
00:18:54,151 --> 00:18:56,381
Think about all the money and time we've invested.

343
00:18:56,381 --> 00:18:59,851
Prove it was all worth it with your results.

344
00:18:59,951 --> 00:19:01,961
Don't worry. I'm your daughter, after all.

345
00:19:02,021 --> 00:19:03,661
Studying abroad is one thing,

346
00:19:03,991 --> 00:19:06,431
but don't try to win just based on your background.

347
00:19:07,161 --> 00:19:08,661
As the owner's daughter,

348
00:19:08,831 --> 00:19:11,801
that background could also be your greatest weakness.

349
00:19:12,231 --> 00:19:13,531
What are you talking about?

350
00:19:13,531 --> 00:19:16,441
As the owner's daughter, she ought to crush the competition.

351
00:19:16,841 --> 00:19:19,211
No matter what it takes,

352
00:19:19,671 --> 00:19:22,841
she should stand out and outperform everyone.

353
00:19:23,641 --> 00:19:25,011
In this day and age,

354
00:19:25,081 --> 00:19:27,651
don't you know the owner's family has to be more careful?

355
00:19:28,821 --> 00:19:31,351
If you can't win based on genuine skill,

356
00:19:31,921 --> 00:19:33,651
then using other means...

357
00:19:33,851 --> 00:19:35,961
is just a blatant abuse of authority.

358
00:19:37,791 --> 00:19:38,791
I'm sure...

359
00:19:39,491 --> 00:19:41,761
you're not actually encouraging her to abuse it.

360
00:19:49,341 --> 00:19:51,141
I have a meeting, so please excuse me.

361
00:20:00,281 --> 00:20:02,021
CEO Kang.

362
00:20:03,451 --> 00:20:04,521
Just a moment.

363
00:20:05,291 --> 00:20:07,121
Your tie is crooked.

364
00:20:12,061 --> 00:20:13,431
What the Chairman said,

365
00:20:14,131 --> 00:20:15,961
don't take it to heart.

366
00:20:16,701 --> 00:20:19,101
You know she didn't mean it.

367
00:20:21,571 --> 00:20:24,171
It's impossible to know what she's really thinking.

368
00:20:33,151 --> 00:20:34,181
There.

369
00:20:35,181 --> 00:20:36,881
Well, have a good day.

370
00:20:41,091 --> 00:20:42,161
Right.

371
00:20:54,841 --> 00:20:57,171
- It's almost time. - Oh, sure.

372
00:21:00,271 --> 00:21:02,141
- Let's go. - What should we get?

373
00:21:02,441 --> 00:21:03,441
Just a minute.

374
00:21:04,811 --> 00:21:07,981
Someone else is joining us for lunch today.

375
00:21:08,781 --> 00:21:10,881
Who? A friend of yours?

376
00:21:14,121 --> 00:21:15,121
Mom.

377
00:21:16,061 --> 00:21:17,091
Hey.

378
00:21:17,631 --> 00:21:19,591
- Have you been waiting long? - Yes.

379
00:21:20,331 --> 00:21:22,001
I'm hungry.

380
00:21:23,901 --> 00:21:26,271
The one joining us was Ms. Park?

381
00:21:29,101 --> 00:21:30,271
You again?

382
00:21:31,741 --> 00:21:34,341
Come on. Do you dislike me that much?

383
00:21:37,581 --> 00:21:40,781
Why? Why do you dislike me so much?

384
00:21:43,251 --> 00:21:45,091
All right, let's go. I'm starving.

385
00:21:45,991 --> 00:21:47,591
Mom, let's go. I'm hungry.

386
00:21:47,791 --> 00:21:48,791
Let's go.

387
00:21:50,391 --> 00:21:52,431
Hey, it's the nice lady!

388
00:21:52,761 --> 00:21:55,761
- Nice lady! - How have you been?

389
00:21:56,031 --> 00:21:58,171
Nice lady, did you come looking for me?

390
00:21:58,531 --> 00:22:00,901
How did you know I was here?

391
00:22:01,941 --> 00:22:05,241
I came with my Seok Jin.

392
00:22:14,821 --> 00:22:15,821
What the heck?

393
00:22:16,281 --> 00:22:18,321
How do they know each other?

394
00:22:20,191 --> 00:22:22,761
Nice lady, this is for you.

395
00:22:25,091 --> 00:22:29,201
Oh, it's so pretty. Thank you so much.

396
00:22:29,861 --> 00:22:31,001
Do you like it?

397
00:22:31,701 --> 00:22:32,701
Yes.

398
00:22:34,701 --> 00:22:37,341
Here, try some of this.

399
00:22:44,481 --> 00:22:45,781
The meat looks delicious too.

400
00:22:46,151 --> 00:22:47,281
Try the meat as well.

401
00:22:49,221 --> 00:22:50,281
Ms. Park!

402
00:22:52,221 --> 00:22:54,391
Nice lady, dig in.

403
00:22:54,891 --> 00:22:56,291
Sure, you too.

404
00:23:04,901 --> 00:23:05,901
There.

405
00:23:08,341 --> 00:23:09,341
Thanks, Seok Jin.

406
00:23:22,151 --> 00:23:23,381
Try some of this.

407
00:23:23,381 --> 00:23:26,021
Hey, I love fish.

408
00:23:30,221 --> 00:23:31,361
It's delicious.

409
00:23:42,201 --> 00:23:43,201
Hey, Ko Eun Seol.

410
00:23:44,001 --> 00:23:45,411
I bet you approached her on purpose.

411
00:23:46,141 --> 00:23:47,541
Knowing she was Seok Jin's mom,

412
00:23:47,611 --> 00:23:49,681
you deliberately helped her, didn't you?

413
00:23:50,041 --> 00:23:52,351
I just ran into her on the street.

414
00:23:57,021 --> 00:23:58,191
Aren't you going to take that off?

415
00:24:00,021 --> 00:24:02,091
Why? I like it.

416
00:24:02,861 --> 00:24:04,021
It suits me.

417
00:24:04,691 --> 00:24:05,861
Though perhaps not you.

418
00:24:09,731 --> 00:24:10,731
Seriously?

419
00:24:14,571 --> 00:24:15,671
Can we talk?

420
00:24:20,771 --> 00:24:21,781
Thanks.

421
00:24:22,441 --> 00:24:23,441
It was nothing.

422
00:24:23,811 --> 00:24:25,851
Anyone would've helped in that situation.

423
00:24:29,281 --> 00:24:30,651
You're still carrying around that keyring.

424
00:24:31,221 --> 00:24:32,221
You can take it off now.

425
00:24:32,751 --> 00:24:33,751
No way.

426
00:24:35,021 --> 00:24:37,491
Doesn't it suit me? I like it.

427
00:24:37,861 --> 00:24:40,391
Your mother seems to know my taste perfectly.

428
00:24:42,161 --> 00:24:43,301
Yes, it suits you.

429
00:24:45,331 --> 00:24:46,631
I really envy you.

430
00:24:49,141 --> 00:24:52,271
You're lucky to have a mother who's so innocent and pure.

431
00:24:56,341 --> 00:24:58,051
When you have a mother like that,

432
00:24:58,681 --> 00:25:00,111
no matter how tough things get,

433
00:25:01,181 --> 00:25:02,851
you can always manage to keep a bright smile.

434
00:25:07,721 --> 00:25:08,791
Thank you.

435
00:25:11,761 --> 00:25:12,961
I should be the one thanking you.

436
00:25:14,361 --> 00:25:15,801
Thanks to you,

437
00:25:15,801 --> 00:25:18,301
I felt like a kid again today which made me happy.

438
00:25:21,301 --> 00:25:22,301
So, are you going somewhere?

439
00:25:22,741 --> 00:25:23,771
I'll be working outside the office.

440
00:25:24,341 --> 00:25:26,311
I feel like my design is missing something.

441
00:25:27,671 --> 00:25:30,011
Gosh. I'll be on my way, then.

442
00:25:30,111 --> 00:25:31,141
Sure.

443
00:25:36,381 --> 00:25:39,721
(PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

444
00:25:44,461 --> 00:25:46,061
- Yes. - Ma'am,

445
00:25:47,231 --> 00:25:50,361
I've found something huge.

446
00:25:52,801 --> 00:25:53,901
What did you say?

447
00:25:54,501 --> 00:25:56,741
(Recording.mp4)

448
00:26:05,481 --> 00:26:06,951
I mean, with this,

449
00:26:07,251 --> 00:26:09,621
there's no connecting the dots. It's pretty obvious.

450
00:26:11,081 --> 00:26:13,821
How did you find this?

451
00:26:14,191 --> 00:26:17,521
Well, that day, this Bae Jong Min guy...

452
00:26:17,791 --> 00:26:19,431
went to the university, home, and the sauna.

453
00:26:19,961 --> 00:26:21,761
I figured it'd be nothing out of the ordinary,

454
00:26:21,861 --> 00:26:23,761
but then he went to the library.

455
00:26:24,571 --> 00:26:27,431
I thought he'd just read a bit and leave,

456
00:26:27,501 --> 00:26:29,041
and I was about to pack it in,

457
00:26:29,801 --> 00:26:32,311
but he kept loitering in the parking lot.

458
00:26:32,741 --> 00:26:33,971
So I went over to see, and...

459
00:26:35,481 --> 00:26:36,481
This is what he was up to.

460
00:26:38,211 --> 00:26:39,211
All right.

461
00:26:39,481 --> 00:26:42,121
For now, don't make any moves without my instruction.

462
00:26:42,221 --> 00:26:43,951
- Got it. - I'll send the payment right away.

463
00:26:45,191 --> 00:26:46,551
Right.

464
00:26:53,091 --> 00:26:54,861
Thank you.

465
00:26:59,471 --> 00:27:03,071
Look. See those people walking down there?

466
00:27:03,701 --> 00:27:05,241
Look closely at how they walk.

467
00:27:06,141 --> 00:27:07,811
Their shoes might seem standard,

468
00:27:07,811 --> 00:27:09,541
but everyone walks differently.

469
00:27:10,811 --> 00:27:13,351
People who walk splay-footed like that?

470
00:27:14,051 --> 00:27:18,721
Their shoe soles, like on this one, get worn down on one side.

471
00:27:19,321 --> 00:27:21,121
That means their pelvis is misaligned...

472
00:27:21,461 --> 00:27:24,191
or they're dealing with a slipped disc.

473
00:27:24,691 --> 00:27:26,261
What else? Please tell me more.

474
00:27:27,191 --> 00:27:28,201
All right.

475
00:27:28,831 --> 00:27:30,901
When the inner sole, like this one,

476
00:27:30,961 --> 00:27:33,701
or the area near the big toe is worn flat,

477
00:27:33,971 --> 00:27:35,471
it points to flat feet...

478
00:27:36,201 --> 00:27:38,771
or a problem with their ankle joints.

479
00:27:40,571 --> 00:27:43,041
- That's so fascinating. - You think so?

480
00:27:43,541 --> 00:27:45,811
That's because you only see shoes...

481
00:27:45,881 --> 00:27:48,351
as fashion or an object.

482
00:27:49,281 --> 00:27:51,321
Then how should I see them?

483
00:27:52,051 --> 00:27:54,921
How well do they support your gait?

484
00:27:55,721 --> 00:27:57,821
That's the basis of a good shoe.

485
00:27:58,491 --> 00:28:01,131
Is walking properly that important?

486
00:28:01,601 --> 00:28:04,201
Shoes should properly support your feet...

487
00:28:05,271 --> 00:28:08,171
and help you keep your balance when you walk.

488
00:28:08,971 --> 00:28:10,971
Are you saying that wearing proper shoes...

489
00:28:11,271 --> 00:28:13,041
can actually fix the way we walk?

490
00:28:13,341 --> 00:28:14,411
That's right.

491
00:28:14,471 --> 00:28:17,981
If you wear shoes that help you walk properly,

492
00:28:18,151 --> 00:28:20,081
your walking habits will change.

493
00:28:21,551 --> 00:28:22,781
I see.

494
00:28:23,581 --> 00:28:25,521
"How to help people walk properly."

495
00:28:44,941 --> 00:28:45,941
Ko Eun Seol?

496
00:28:48,011 --> 00:28:49,881
Gosh, I'm sorry.

497
00:28:59,051 --> 00:29:00,051
Eun Seol?

498
00:29:04,091 --> 00:29:05,131
Ms. Joo?

499
00:29:07,961 --> 00:29:08,961
Are you all right?

500
00:29:21,341 --> 00:29:22,341
I'm fine.

501
00:29:29,851 --> 00:29:30,921
Eun Seol.

502
00:29:48,871 --> 00:29:52,041
You're very uncomfortable around me, aren't you, Eun Seol?

503
00:29:59,751 --> 00:30:02,851
I was the person closest to Manager Na,

504
00:30:03,951 --> 00:30:04,951
and you...

505
00:30:06,091 --> 00:30:09,121
suffered for the past ten years because of him.

506
00:30:10,191 --> 00:30:11,221
You have every right to feel that way.

507
00:30:16,801 --> 00:30:19,331
But did you know?

508
00:30:21,001 --> 00:30:22,741
I was one of Manager Na's victims too.

509
00:30:24,301 --> 00:30:25,311
What?

510
00:30:27,071 --> 00:30:28,481
Because of Manager Na,

511
00:30:29,341 --> 00:30:31,181
I lost a dear friend.

512
00:30:32,651 --> 00:30:33,751
Really?

513
00:30:35,051 --> 00:30:37,751
Hee Jung was such a wonderful person.

514
00:30:41,051 --> 00:30:42,121
Wait.

515
00:30:42,861 --> 00:30:44,461
You knew my mom?

516
00:30:47,261 --> 00:30:49,661
The whole thing with Manager Na is how I found out...

517
00:30:50,831 --> 00:30:53,731
that your mother was Hee Jung.

518
00:30:56,641 --> 00:30:58,911
Hee Jung and I went to the same high school.

519
00:30:59,611 --> 00:31:00,911
Same school, same class.

520
00:31:02,741 --> 00:31:03,741
Wait.

521
00:31:04,981 --> 00:31:06,311
How can this be?

522
00:31:09,381 --> 00:31:10,381
That's why...

523
00:31:12,451 --> 00:31:15,091
it was even harder for me to face you.

524
00:31:21,831 --> 00:31:24,231
Hee Jung was such a wonderful person.

525
00:31:25,571 --> 00:31:28,641
She loved poetry and spring...

526
00:31:31,241 --> 00:31:32,471
Ms. Joo.

527
00:31:38,951 --> 00:31:42,581
From now on, if you have any trouble at the company, lean on me.

528
00:31:43,881 --> 00:31:46,991
I may not be able to replace your mom,

529
00:31:47,851 --> 00:31:50,761
but as her friend, I want to help you.

530
00:32:15,921 --> 00:32:18,891
I'll be there for you.

531
00:32:34,871 --> 00:32:36,271
Thank you so much,

532
00:32:37,001 --> 00:32:38,071
Ms. Joo.

533
00:33:07,531 --> 00:33:11,241
(A Trap Called Desire)

534
00:33:11,301 --> 00:33:13,041
I need to keep her close by my side...

535
00:33:13,171 --> 00:33:15,481
and keep her on a leash to tame her.

536
00:33:15,711 --> 00:33:18,281
Don't worry. I can easily beat someone like Ko Eun Seol.

537
00:33:18,381 --> 00:33:19,781
Where did you get this?

538
00:33:20,011 --> 00:33:23,251
Eun Seol, you have fought through so much hardship and adversity.

539
00:33:23,351 --> 00:33:25,421
I want someone like you to prove what you're capable of.

540
00:33:25,721 --> 00:33:26,721
Ma'am.

541
00:33:27,221 --> 00:33:28,821
- I'm off. - Where are you going?

542
00:33:28,821 --> 00:33:30,321
Did you get a job?

543
00:33:31,061 --> 00:33:33,661
No matter what she tries, she's still beneath my feet.

544
00:33:33,931 --> 00:33:36,761
I'm so sick of people talking about Ko Eun Seol everywhere I go.

545
00:33:36,961 --> 00:33:39,571
I couldn't stand seeing Ko Eun Seol act like she owned the place,

546
00:33:39,931 --> 00:33:41,231
so I did something foolish.

547
00:33:42,241 --> 00:33:43,241
You did something reckless?
